<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02044</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>eceb67de-cd1c-4eba-b2f3-e0cd3812958b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will determine what expressions would produce graphs with particular vertices. We will look more closely at how changing the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>k</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in a quadratic expression of the form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>–</m:mo><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>k</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> translates the graph, and recall that the coefficient <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> affects the direction of the opening of a parabola.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Describe how changing a number in the vertex form of a quadratic function affects its graph.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>7.17.1: Quadratic Expressions in Different Forms</item>
  <item>7.17.2: Modify Expressions to Translate Graphs <list id="list-00003">
    <item>7.17.2: Self Check</item>
    <item>7.17.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>

  <item>7.17.3: Changing the Parameters of a Quadratic Expression<list id="list-00004">
    <item>7.17.3: Self Check</item>
    <item>7.17.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
  
  <item>7.17.4: Transforming the Parent Function</item>
  <item>7.17.5: Equations of Graph Translations</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review.</emphasis></para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>7.17.6: Practice</item>
  <item>7.17.7: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
